1
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:09,044
SHIT, IT'S DARK IN HERE,
CAN'T SEE A DAMN THING,

2
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,700
WHERE THE HELL IS THAT BASTARD ANYWAY?

3
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:23,117
IT'S THE MIDDLE OF THE DAY AND I STILL
HAVE TO FEEL MY WAY AROUND THIS HOVEL,

4
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,612
THIS BETTER BE WORTH IT.

5
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:29,860
Okay, if I remember correctly,
I'll find Dio over in that room.

6
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:40,057
Disgusting, this little lady
must be one of Dio's leftovers!

7
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:42,697
Damn bras just throw
themselves at the guy.

8
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,617
Like having their blood drank
is the latest bedroom craze.

9
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:47,957
The whole thing's nutty if you ask me?

10
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,980
Though girls do tend
to go for the bad boys.

11
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,140
But forget about that.

12
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,237
I've never seen so much gold in my life.

13
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:56,614
How'd he get all this?

14
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:01,091
It seems like this guy can have
and do just about anything.

15
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:09,970
Horse.

16
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,560
What is it?

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:22,830
It's...

18
00:01:22,913 --> 00:01:23,743
Master... Dio.

19
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:32,600
Son of a bitch. What is this?

20
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:36,331
Just looking at him is enough
to send chills down my spine.

21
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,117
Keep it together, whole horse.

22
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,612
Don't let him spook you.

23
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:44,117
He's nothing to lose your cool over.

24
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,024
Yeah, he's not even that
much stronger than you.

25
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,500
I'll ask you again.

26
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:52,540
Did you want something, whole horns?

27
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,780
Uh, well, yes, actually.

28
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:57,217
There's something I
thought you ought to know.

29
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,777
I received intel that two
of the nine great gods,

30
00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:02,357
Mariah and Alessi, have
been put out of commission.

31
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:03,920
And your point is?

32
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:06,360
Well, there's more.

33
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,071
We've got trouble coming.

34
00:02:08,340 --> 00:02:11,217
Turns out Joestar and his gang
will arrive in Cairo tomorrow,

35
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,712
and only three of the nine gods are left.

36
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:16,291
It seems you've misunderstood my question.

37
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:19,699
I want to know what you're
going to do, whole horse.

38
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,257
You seem to have been
caught rather off guard.

39
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:26,222
I simply wish to know when you're
going to kill them, whole horse.

40
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:29,257
While it's true you've
pledged your allegiance to me,

41
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:32,800
you have yet to adequately
prove yourself in battle.

42
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:37,620
In this day and age, any
simpleton can deliver information.

43
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:42,600
Twice you've failed me, and
here you are crawling back.

44
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,380
You couldn't know this,

45
00:02:57,540 --> 00:03:01,217
but my body once belonged to a man
by the name of Jonathan Joestar.

46
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:04,860
Jonathan was the grandfather
of Joseph Joestar.

47
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:07,017
Look closely.

48
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:10,924
Notice how the left finger heals
at a slower rate than the right.

49
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:14,380
The left side of this body is weak,

50
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:17,980
which proves that it doesn't
completely belong to me yet.

51
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,280
And that I am not yet immortal.

52
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:24,520
I am ill-equipped to fight a battle
with Joestar and his friends.

53
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:34,560
Now then, if there is nothing else, run
along and destroy my enemies on my behalf.

54
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:39,020
Failure will most assuredly
result in your untimely demise.

55
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:41,577
You're burking up the wrong tree, Haas.

56
00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:45,601
As if threats are gonna make me
roll over and do whatever you want.

57
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,000
On your behalf, my ass?

58
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:49,720
I'm no fool.

59
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,937
I'm smart enough to throw
in with whoever's strongest.

60
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:55,297
Everything I've said has been lip service.

61
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:58,733
I'd never swear my loyalty to
you at the cost of my soul.

62
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,100
Rat bastard, you're not so tough, are you?

63
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,820
You're wide open.

64
00:04:04,060 --> 00:04:08,337
Guess having another person's body
attached to your head has made you go soft.

65
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,600
This is perfect.

66
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:12,117
I don't have to fight
Joseph and the other three.

67
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:14,494
Not when I've got Dio in my crosshairs.

68
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:19,724
It'd be a hell of a lot easier to blow his
head to smithereens right here and now.

69
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:25,031
If I do, his treasures mine for the Taken.

70
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,808
This'll be a piece of cake.

71
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:29,997
He doesn't know Emperor's
aimed point blank at his skull.

72
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:32,717
I can finish him off and
he'll be none the wiser.

73
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:36,388
Just one pull of the trigger
and this nightmare will be over.

74
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,118
After all, Emperor was made
for close combat carnage.

75
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,180
I can do this.

76
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:42,240
I can do this.

77
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:44,000
Is there a problem?

78
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,717
You seem to be hesitating.

79
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,820
Eat lead, shitbag!

80
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:52,480
I'm about to splatter your brains
all over the floor, Mr. Dio!

81
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:56,153
Are you positive you want to
go through with shooting me?

82
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:02,360
He's gone!

83
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,350
Fascinating.

84
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:10,117
As you prepared to fire,
your breathing was relaxed.

85
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,040
You didn't even perspire.

86
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:13,617
You were composed.

87
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:16,080
Very impressive, whole horse.

88
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,517
This doesn't make a lick of sense.

89
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:31,440
I didn't even see him move.

90
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,877
There's no way in hell he
could have creeped up behind

91
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:37,136
me without breaking a single
one of those spider webs.

92
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,110
Fast or not,

93
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:41,837
he shouldn't have been able to sneak up
to my rear without me noticing something.

94
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:45,200
Was that the power of Dio's stand?

95
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:49,020
The power of the world,
ill-equipped? Yeah, right.

96
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:54,597
I finally understand, Master Dio.

97
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:58,217
I've got no choice but to pledge
my eternal loyalty to you.

98
00:05:58,300 --> 00:05:59,760
You've got me beat.

99
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:13,780
I'll wake you in the morning.

100
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,820
In the end of the day of the world,

101
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:29,220
I'm afraid of the devil!

102
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:31,297
I'm afraid of the devil?

103
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:32,660
I'm afraid of him.

104
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:39,817
I'm afraid of him, I'm afraid of him.

105
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:42,200
The end of the day to the end.

106
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:44,580
You can beat the world.

107
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:46,930
Stop.

108
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,550
Get down.

109
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,260
When it's been started,

110
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:55,957
I'm at the moment of being lost.

111
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:59,700
I'm going to continue to keep going.

112
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:02,557
Stop, stop, stop.

113
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:04,857
No last page.

114
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:06,440
The

115
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:11,290
Yeah

116
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:12,690
Yeah Yeah

117
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:18,320
Yeah Yeah Yeah Yeah

118
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:40,317
Ladies and gentlemen, we sincerely hope
you've enjoyed today's flight from Aswan.

119
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:44,459
We'll be arriving on schedule at
Cairo International Airport shortly.

120
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:00,760
Whoops, snooze you lose, buddy!

121
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:05,614
I hate to break it to you, cowboy,
but it looks like this is our cab now.

122
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:07,960
No hard feelings.

123
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:09,510
Huh?

124
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:12,895
Don't tell me you're going
to start crying like a baby!

125
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:18,790
Shit!

126
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:20,340
What the hell?!

127
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,400
Giza Pronto.

128
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,934
The Minoru House Hotel.

129
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:35,557
I'm gonna open up this
suitcase and let you out.

130
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:38,697
Unless you want some Card
pain, I suggest you keep calm.

131
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:39,740
We clear? Huh?

132
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:42,077
Did you, uh, say something just now, sir?

133
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:44,297
If I did, it sure the hell wasn't to you.

134
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:46,145
Now shut up and drive the cab!

135
00:08:46,660 --> 00:08:47,490
Yes, sir.

136
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:58,920
Cut it out.

137
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:01,257
You know, if you weren't
making such a damn racket,

138
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:05,037
I wouldn't have had to hogtie you and put
you on the plane like a piece of luggage.

139
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,800
Don't be a baby, Mondatta.

140
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:10,037
Your brother's got another month in
the hospital thanks to that bomb,

141
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,649
so you and I are partners.

142
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:15,217
Now make sure those big ears are listening,
because here's what we're going to do.

143
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:16,857
We're going to use your
book of premonitions

144
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:19,293
and my assassin gun to stamp out Jotaro,

145
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,497
Joseph, and the rest of those SOBs.

146
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:22,698
Got that, Mondatta?

147
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,217
I get that we haven't
known each other long?

148
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:26,337
But from what I've gathered,

149
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:29,877
You're afraid of just about anyone
that's not your brother Zenyatta.

150
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:33,237
But don't you think this is the
perfect chance to avenge the guy?

151
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:36,137
You don't want to be a
yellow-bellied coward forever, right?

152
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:37,102
That's no good.

153
00:09:37,460 --> 00:09:38,872
I'm out of options, too.

154
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,901
We've got no choice but to fight.

155
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:43,632
Time for us to get our revenge, Mondatta.

156
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,917
I'm gonna let you loose now,

157
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,597
but you have to swear to me you won't
carry on with all that infernal hollering,

158
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:50,510
okay?

159
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:52,940
See that, son?

160
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:54,380
I'm not so bad.

161
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,306
Now try and settle down, huh?

162
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:58,497
I don't need you getting sick on me.

163
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:01,757
Because believe it or not, I'm
on your side in this whole mess.

164
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:02,958
So don't you worry.

165
00:10:03,220 --> 00:10:04,420
Just relax for now.

166
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:09,570
Huh?

167
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:15,520
Sir, why do you have
a puking kid? Shut up!

168
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:17,500
I see.

169
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:20,702
You got Moshe's sickness
from being on the plane.

170
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,360
Mondatta, let's be pals from here on.

171
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:25,560
How's that sound?

172
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:30,500
I'm Mondatta.

173
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:32,040
This is Whole Horse.

174
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:34,380
He's mean and I don't like him.

175
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:38,757
While Mondatta was sleeping, Whole Horse
tied him up and stuffed him in a trunk.

176
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:41,097
Mondatta was taken from
his brother Zenyatta.

177
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:42,140
He was sad.

178
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:45,057
But even though Mondatta
was scared out of his mind,

179
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:46,817
he wanted to avenge his brother.

180
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:49,606
So he decided to work
up his co - Whole Horse.

181
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:53,660
Oh, come on.

182
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:54,937
You won't even get near me?

183
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:59,020
Well, I guess you're trying which
is all I can ask for at this point

184
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,100
And by the way,

185
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:02,657
I gotta know does your
stand really predict the

186
00:11:02,740 --> 00:11:05,377
future or is that just
some cockamamie rumor?

187
00:11:05,460 --> 00:11:09,137
If that was all just a tall tale,
then I brought you here for nothing.

188
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:12,573
I mean even with it your
brother got blown to high heaven

189
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:14,521
Which is it kid?

190
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:15,641
Are you a fraud?

191
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:22,277
How'd a new comic appear on a
blank page from out of nowhere?

192
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:25,957
While Mondatta and Whole Horse were
walking through the outskirts of Cairo,

193
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:29,137
they met a lady who was as
pretty as the day was long.

194
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:32,520
Then Whole Horse jump-kicked
the lady in the neck! Hmm?

195
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:35,737
The pretty lady was so
overjoyed about the kick that,

196
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:38,137
out of the blue, she gave
Whole Horse her jewels!

197
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,680
Yahoo! We're rich!

198
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:42,987
What the hell is this crap?!

199
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:46,257
You must think I was born last night!

200
00:11:46,340 --> 00:11:48,057
You call this a prediction, Mondatta?

201
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:49,320
There's just no way!

202
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:51,397
This crap has to be made up or something.

203
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:53,180
I'm telling the truth.

204
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,640
I stand, boss.

205
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:57,292
You just have to trust in its prophecies.

206
00:11:57,900 --> 00:11:59,117
They're... they're...

207
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,297
they're 100.

208
00:12:00,380 --> 00:12:02,917
They're 100 % right every time.

209
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,597
They're right 100 %?!

210
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,557
You trying to pull a wool over my eyes?!

211
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:08,637
There's no way some
lady's gonna give me her

212
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:10,837
jewels after jump kicking her in the neck.

213
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:14,685
You'd have to be off your rocker
to do something like that, hmm?

214
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:25,437
Listen, Mondatta, I'm proud
to say that I'm a gentleman,

215
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:27,037
and a proper gentleman at that.

216
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:29,377
Because at that, I got
girls all over the world.

217
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:33,117
I might tell a white lie now and again,
but I'd never haul off and hit one.

218
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:37,847
I respect all the ladies, the beauties,
the plain ones, and even the ugly ones.

219
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:42,357
There's no way your prediction
will ever come to pass.

220
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:45,717
Come hell or high water, I
swear I will never hit a woman.

221
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:48,417
She could pay me every dime,
nickel, and quarter she had.

222
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,957
I still wouldn't put my hands on her.

223
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:52,360
It's 100 % true, yes.

224
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:01,360
See there?

225
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:03,422
Your fancy prediction was wrong.

226
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:22,570
Ah!

227
00:13:22,653 --> 00:13:23,635
Who the hell are you?

228
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:29,717
What in the...

229
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:32,200
There was a scorpion in your shawl.

230
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:35,174
This thing's sting is a death sentence.

231
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:36,090
What?

232
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:41,737
You spotted that wretched creature before
it had a chance to crawl into my clothes.

233
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:45,349
If you hadn't killed it, she
would have been stung for sure.

234
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:48,037
You saved my life.

235
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:50,120
Oh, please, let me repay you.

236
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:52,657
Would my necklace be a sufficient reward?

237
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:53,570
It's yours.

238
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:58,360
Boy, this is my lucky day.

239
00:13:58,900 --> 00:14:00,857
Mountain and I are practically invincible.

240
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:02,646
We'll be the unstoppable duo.

241
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:14,377
I don't think I'm going to
be able to help you, folks.

242
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:18,600
It's been my job to repair rooftops
in Cairo for around 40 years now.

243
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,497
And I can't say that I've
ever seen a place like this.

244
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:23,497
From the looks of the building's design,

245
00:14:23,580 --> 00:14:26,057
the thing was built over
a hundred years ago,

246
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:26,970
give or take.

247
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:29,777
If I had to take a guess,
based on the picture,

248
00:14:29,860 --> 00:14:32,297
I'd say you'd find it
somewhere south of here.

249
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:36,237
The buildings in Cairo get older and
older the farther south you travel.

250
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:37,150
Huh?

